Package: baeconstrat
Type: Package
Title: Macro-to-Balance-Sheet Strategy Analytics for South African Banks
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Rossouw", "van Jaarsveld", email = "rossouwvanjaarsveld@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Ties macroeconomic scenarios to a bank's balance sheet, earnings and
    return on equity using public South African Reserve Bank data. A two-stage
    top-down design first links macro variables to the aggregate banking sector
    (BA100/BA120/BA200/BA700 sector returns, BA900 totals), then links individual
    banks to the sector (BA900 bank-level balance sheets: growth betas, market
    shares and regime asymmetries). A fictional bank, No Gut Feelings Bank (NGFB),
    is drawn from the posterior predictive of a hierarchical model of the large
    banks and embedded in the sector. Scenario projections feed a net-interest,
    credit-loss, cost and capital engine, macro sensitivities and a pre-positioning
    optimiser that recommends balance-sheet moves ahead of a scenario, reported in
    ROE and net income. Model checks (Clark-West, bounds tests, asymmetric
    pass-through, convex credit losses, forecast combination) test the Stage 1
    models against alternatives on the footing they are used on. A monthly
    layer disaggregates quarterly macro series with the Kalman filter and
    compares monthly and quarterly satellites, polynomial distributed lags and
    Bayesian shrinkage on the same outcomes, with simulated dynamic
    multipliers and local projections. Market-share strategy (where a bank
    under-participates in each macro regime, and what closing the gap is worth
    at the margin) and macro-adjusted performance measurement (par and frontier
    share performance against the large-bank population) complete it.
